# Normalize line endings on commit. Checkout uses LF by default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Quartus II runs on Windows and writes CRLF. It reads these files back.
# -text stores and checks out these files byte for byte, with no end-of-line
# conversion in either direction. The files stay exactly as Quartus II wrote
# them, and git records no change when a Windows and a Linux checkout differ.
*.vhd -text
*.bdf -text
*.vwf -text
*.qsf -text

# Documents
*.md text eol=lf

# Binary. Git must not attempt a line-ending conversion or a text diff.
*.pdf binary
